    "summary": "Incendiary Alligator>Other One and soaring Not Fade Away finale",
    "blurb": "Show opens with a crisp Cold Rain And Snow before launching into an incendiary Alligator > The Other One stretch. The second set delivers a soaring Not Fade Away climax and tight Garcia‑Weir interplay. Recording is fair‑quality audience tape but captures the raw 1970 energy.",
    "review": "On July 10, 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead were in full‑tilt early‑70 mode, trading the polished studio sheen of later years for a gritty, live‑room feel that still manages to thrill. The set kicks off with a bright Cold Rain And Snow and quickly dives into an explosive Alligator → The Other One sequence, complete with a wild drum break that lets Mickey’s snare hiccup but keeps the momentum rolling. A highlight comes when the band weaves through Attics Of My Life before slipping into Cryptical Envelopment and Cosmic Charlie, showcasing their knack for seamless segues. The night closes on an uplifting Not Fade Away where Garcia’s soaring lead intertwines with Bob’s vocal‑guitar “mind‑meld,” delivering a finale that feels both intimate and expansive despite the tape’s cloudy ambience. While crowd chatter and occasional mic bleed remind you it’s a raw audience recording, the performance itself is a vivid snapshot of the Dead at the top of their improvisational game in 1970.",
